1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.966
Every day, useful plans disappear into screenshots.

2
00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:05.994
A live event in LINE.

3
00:00:05.994 --> 00:00:07.869
A workshop on X.

4
00:00:07.869 --> 00:00:10.331
A reservation sent in a chat.

5
00:00:10.331 --> 00:00:13.290
We save the image... and still miss the date.

6
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.471
SnapCal closes that gap.

7
00:00:15.471 --> 00:00:19.706
Take a screenshot, and it becomes a calendar event in seconds.

8
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:21.454
There are two ways to use it.

9
00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.663
For maximum privacy, share one image directly to SnapCal.

10
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:30.969
Or, when you choose, start monitoring and keep the small bubble at the edge of the screen.

11
00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:35.357
The moment a new screenshot arrives, the bubble shows the progress.

12
00:00:35.357 --> 00:00:39.566
Here is the important part: the screenshot never leaves the phone.

13
00:00:39.566 --> 00:00:44.808
Japanese OCR, date extraction, and safety checks all run on device.

14
00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:46.007
No account.

15
00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:47.882
No API key.

16
00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:49.987
No cloud image upload.

17
00:00:49.987 --> 00:00:57.499
SnapCal only adds an event when it finds exactly one clear title, one future date, and one start time.

18
00:00:57.499 --> 00:01:00.931
If the screenshot is ambiguous, it does nothing.

19
00:01:00.931 --> 00:01:03.290
That restraint is the superpower.

20
00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.492
SnapCal is designed not to pollute your calendar.

21
00:01:06.492 --> 00:01:15.369
When the event is clear, SnapCal adds it to the calendar you selected, including a Google Calendar synced with Android, and sets a thirty-minute reminder.

22
00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:21.364
Every result has its own Undo action, so SnapCal can remove only the event it created.

23
00:01:21.364 --> 00:01:28.176
We used Codex and GPT-5.6 to design, build, test, and harden this flow.

24
00:01:28.176 --> 00:01:31.632
But no cloud AI runs inside the installed app.

25
00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:41.594
SnapCal turns the moment, “I should remember this,” into, “It is already on my calendar” — privately, safely, and almost instantly.
